description:
Sites in chat-server (clippy::single_match_else, 13 hits in src/):
- ban.rs:130, ban.rs:141, ban.rs:182, ban.rs:233, ban.rs:247
- chat.rs:402
- contact.rs:164, contact.rs:187
- emoji.rs:448, emoji.rs:462
- message.rs:530
- position.rs:226
- presence.rs:165
- space.rs:896, space.rs:931, space.rs:949 (already cited in JMAP-x2gd.55 for items_after_statements; the match-shape is the separate complaint)

Mail-server has 7 hits of the same pattern in its lib (canonical sibling).

Shape:

    let space_id = match obj_val.get("spaceId").and_then(|v| v.as_str()) {
        Some(s) => Id::from(s),
        None => {
            not_created.insert(create_id, SetError::invalid_properties()...);
            continue;
        }
    };

This is the classic 'let-else with side-effecting else' shape. Pure let-else handles the trivial Some(s) => s case (which is what JMAP-x2gd.54 / manual_let_else covers), but here the else arm contains a side effect (insert + continue), so let-else doesn't apply directly.

What idiomatic Rust does for this shape: two equivalent rewrites, both clearer than match:

(a) Early-return / continue via let-else:
    let Some(s) = obj_val.get("spaceId").and_then(|v| v.as_str()) else {
        not_created.insert(create_id, SetError::invalid_properties()...);
        continue;
    };
    let space_id = Id::from(s);

(b) if-let-else (clippy's preferred suggestion):
    let space_id = if let Some(s) = obj_val.get("spaceId").and_then(|v| v.as_str()) {
        Id::from(s)
    } else {
        not_created.insert(create_id, SetError::invalid_properties()...);
        continue;
    };

(a) is the more modern Rust shape (stable since 1.65, same as let-else for the no-side-effect case in JMAP-x2gd.54).

What goes wrong as-is: same as .54's complaint — readability + paragraph-of-arm-bodies obscures the early-exit control flow. The pattern is dense in /set handlers because they validate 5-10 fields per object before committing the create, so the cumulative cost is real.

Workspace-canonical: 13 chat + 7 mail = 20 sites total. File against the canonical mail-server first per AGENTS.md propagation rule. After mail-server lands, propagate to all extension-server siblings as a single sweep.

Cross-references JMAP-x2gd.54 (manual_let_else for the trivial Some=>s, None=>continue case — 9 sites still open) and JMAP-x2gd.55 (items_after_statements in the same /set handlers).

clippy::pedantic verified 2026-05-16 against current HEAD.
